  "description": "T1 - Mimosa. Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 1-1.5m to create a tidy shape. Remove lower branch.\rT2 - Dead Tree. Remove dead tree.\rT3 - Bay. Reduce height by approx. 2.5m. Trim all around to contain.\rT5-T6 - Hornbeam x2. Reduce all aspects of crowns by approx. 1-1.5m to create a tight and tidy shape.  Lift lower branches to create 2m clearance.\rT7 - Bay. Reduce height by 2m and shape.\rT8 - Cherry. Reduce overlong branch by 2m.\rT9 - Cherry. Reduce overlong branch.\rT10 - Ash. Crown lift to provide 2.5m clearance from ground level. Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 1-1.5m.\rT11 - Robinia. Reduce all aspects of the crown back to previous points of reduction, approx. 1-2m.\rT12 - Cherry. Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 4m. Thin by 10%. Remove deadwood and crossing branches. \rT13 - Hornbeam. Reduce height by approx. 3m and shape.\rT14 - Silver Birch. Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 2m to create a tight and tidy shape.\rT15 - Mimosa. Reduce all aspects of the crown by approx. 1-2m to create a tight and tidy shape. Remove deadwood.",
